cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SARGuardian: measured limits of NISAR L-band SAR for
  Himalayan slope-failure early warning
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sarker
    given-names: Moshiour Rahman
repository-code: https://github.com/moshiour0/SARGuardian
abstract: >-
  A pipeline and measurement campaign testing what NISAR Level-2
  products can and cannot see of a Himalayan slope failure. At the
  Sentinel-2 candidate scar that matches the published detachment
  elevation of the 26 August 2026 Langtang Lirung collapse, NISAR
  ascending offset tracking had a line-of-sight detection floor of
  9.2 mm/day (1 km window median) to 32.0 mm/day (one pixel) in the
  seven weeks before failure: 28 to 96 times the 0.33 mm/day
  precursor Sentinel-1 interferometry measured there. NISAR phase has
  no valid pixel at that candidate in any pair. The failure itself is
  detectable as loss of correlation, at 14-35 times the event-free
  baseline. Winter products are BETA and summer PROVISIONAL, and the
  public archive has no products for January-June 2026; both are
  stated as limits.
keywords:
  - InSAR
  - NISAR
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - offset tracking
  - landslide
  - early warning
  - Himalaya
license: MIT
